{% extends "web_layout.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ brand.name }} — Pricing{% endblock %}
{% block style %}
  {# ------------------------------------------------------------------ pricing
     The page that takes the money: every control here is a link to the Shopify
     store. So this restyle is CSS only — not one href, price string, macro
     branch, data-* hook or aria attribute moved. What changed is the surface
     the sheet was written for: cream gradient cards, a bone-bright table
     header and an orange CTA are all light-field assumptions.

     Two rules shape the whole file:

     - AMBER marks a value the ENGINE MEASURED. On a pricing page there is
       exactly one such value — `trend_line`, the golfer's own before→after
       read from their own sessions. Prices are numbers the STORE charges, the
       savings badge is a claim, and a comparison tick is a plan fact. None of
       them were measured, so none of them are amber. The page is deliberately
       near-monochrome; the single amber strip is the one thing on it the
       product actually computed.
     - Buttons are BONE on the field with a hairline. An amber button would
       read as a metric, and a checkout link is not one.

     EVERY comment below is a Jinja comment, and that is not a style choice.
     A /* */ inside this block is served to the browser verbatim, so a comment
     that quotes page copy puts that copy in the response even when the
     template decided not to render it. That is not hypothetical: quoting the
     annual savings chip here leaked the string into the render with
     billing.pro_annual_badge_text cleared — the stale claim that knob exists
     to remove — and tests/test_membership_tiers.py::
     test_annual_badge_is_a_display_string failed on it. Keep them Jinja. #}
  main { max-width: var(--sl-content); }

  {# ---- lead ----
     Left-aligned and ruled rather than centred: this is the product's own
     price sheet, and an instrument reads down a left edge. #}
  .lead {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    text-align: left;
  }
  {# The shared display rung, not a hand-rolled clamp(). The shell's token
     sheet calls out exactly this: two surfaces that share a typeface and not
     a scale is how they drift apart. #}
  .lead h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4);
    color: var(--sl-green);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
    font-size: var(--sl-heading-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 0.98;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  {# :not(.sl-eyebrow) so the shell's eyebrow keeps its own mono rung — the
     eyebrow is a <p> inside this block too. #}
  .lead p:not(.sl-eyebrow) {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .lead p strong { color: var(--sl-ink); font-weight: 500; }

  {# ---- the golfer's own numbers ----
     THE measured value on this page, rendered only when two sessions of real
     data exist. Amber mono, tabular, on the well — because this is the one
     string here the engine produced rather than the price list. #}
  .personal {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-5);
    padding: var(--sl-space-3) var(--sl-space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sl-accent);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: var(--sl-night);
    color: var(--sl-orange-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-align: left;
  }

  {# ---- the plan ladder ----
     One ruled grid, not a row of floating cards: the rules are drawn by a 1px
     gap over --sl-border, and each panel repaints itself in --sl-bg-card.

     Flex rather than CSS grid on purpose. The card count is 3–6 depending on
     which rungs the store can actually sell (the one-payment pass needs a
     store, the upper tier needs its rollout flag, and its two cards are
     independently gated), and flex grows the last row's items to fill it. A
     grid would leave an empty track in the final row, and an empty cell in
     this construction paints as a solid --sl-border block. #}
  .plans {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1px;
    align-items: stretch;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: var(--sl-border);
    box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-sm);
  }
  {# The shell's .card brings its own border, radius and shadow. Inside a
     ruled grid those double every hairline and round each cell off the grid,
     so they come off here and the 1px gap is the only rule. #}
  .plans .card {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 28px);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--sl-bg-card);
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  .plans h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2);
    color: var(--sl-green);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  {# Bone mono, tabular, and deliberately NOT amber: a price is charged, not
     measured. Weight 500 is the top of the DM Mono family we ship — the old
     800 was a faux bold the browser drew itself. #}
  .price {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4);
    color: var(--sl-ink);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-2xl);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .plans ul {
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-5);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    align-content: start;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  }
  .plans li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--sl-space-3) 0 var(--sl-space-3) var(--sl-space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  {# A square tick, not a dot — and ink, not cyan: the trace colour marks the
     live readout, and a feature list is not one. #}
  .plans li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    top: 1.34em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    background: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  }
  {# The annual savings chip: a claim, not a measurement, so a bone hairline
     rather than the filled green pill it used to be. #}
  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-3);
    padding: 5px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-control-border);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-ink);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  {# ---- the annual hero panel ----
     The deepest well in the grid, with the buy box raised out of it. The old
     treatment was a radial glow, a decorative ring and a 60px drop shadow:
     none of those survive on a near-black field (the shell's shadow tokens
     lead with an inset lit edge for exactly this reason), and none of them
     said anything. Depth carries the hierarchy instead. #}
  .plans .card.hero {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sl-space-5);
    align-items: start;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 40px);
    background: var(--sl-night);
    box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-sm);
  }
  .card.hero h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2);
    color: var(--sl-ink);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-3xl);
  }
  {# One step brighter, because these hairlines sit on the well rather than on
     a panel. #}
  .card.hero ul { margin-bottom: 0; border-top-color: var(--sl-border-strong); }
  .card.hero li { border-bottom-color: var(--sl-border-strong); }
  .hero-plan__buy {
    padding: clamp(18px, 2vw, 24px);
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: var(--sl-bg-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-sm);
  }
  .hero-plan__label {
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2);
    color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .card.hero .price {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-3xl);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  {# ---- checkout controls ----
     The shell's baseline paints `background: var(--sl-green-btn)` with
     `color: white`. Since the inversion --sl-green-btn IS the bone ink, so
     that pairing is bone on bone — an invisible label. Here that is every
     checkout link on the only paid surface the app has, so the ink is
     corrected here to the token that exists for this exact pairing.
     Bone face, field-coloured ink, hairline edge. Never amber. #}
  .plans a.button,
  .plans button {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 46px;
    margin-top: var(--sl-space-4);
    padding: 11px 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-green-btn);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-control);
    background: var(--sl-green-btn);
    color: var(--sl-green-ink);
    box-shadow: none;
    text-align: center;
  }
  {# Hover goes to the trace colour, matching the storefront's primary button
     and the shell's link hover. transform is cleared so nothing here moves —
     the shell's reduced-motion block would neutralise it anyway, but a
     checkout button has no reason to hop under the cursor. #}
  .plans a.button:hover,
  .plans button:hover {
    border-color: var(--sl-ink-hi);
    background: var(--sl-ink-hi);
    color: var(--sl-green-ink);
    transform: none;
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  .plans a.button:active,
  .plans button:active { transform: none; box-shadow: none; }
  {# The buy control sits on the bottom edge of every stacked card so the
     panels line up whatever length their feature list is. The hero's button
     lives inside .hero-plan__buy, which is block flow — auto computes to zero
     there, hence the exclusion. #}
  .plans .card form,
  .plans .card:not(.hero) a.button,
  .plans .card:not(.hero) button { margin-top: auto; }
  .plans .hint {
    margin-top: var(--sl-space-3);
    color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  }
  .plans .hint strong { color: var(--sl-ink); }

  {# ---- the one-payment card ---- #}
  .card.founders { background: var(--sl-bg-card); }
  .founders-cap {
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-3);
    padding: 4px 9px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: var(--sl-orange-soft);
    color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .founders-note {
    margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--sl-space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  {# The unpopulated cell: the free rung sits on the field itself, so the paid
     panels read as the filled ones. Transparent would have shown the grid's
     own --sl-border through, which is why this is the field token. #}
  .plans .card.quiet { background: var(--sl-bg); }

  {# ---- comparison ---- #}
  .compare-section { margin-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); }
  .compare-head { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4); }
  .compare-head h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--sl-green);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
    font-size: var(--sl-heading-support);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.06;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .compare-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
    background: var(--sl-bg-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-sm);
  }
  table.compare { width: 100%; min-width: 680px; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .compare th, .compare td {
    padding: var(--sl-space-3) var(--sl-space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  }
  {# Mono labels on the well. The old rule filled this row with --sl-green,
     which post-inversion is the bone ink — a full-width bone bar would be the
     brightest object on a near-black page, and brightest around the least
     important text on it. #}
  .compare thead th {
    padding: var(--sl-space-3) var(--sl-space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
    background: var(--sl-night);
    color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .compare thead th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  .compare tbody th {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-ink);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .compare tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.022); }
  .compare td {
    color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  {# A tick in this table states a plan fact, not a measured value, so it is
     bone rather than amber. The em dash carries the negative case in text, so
     the distinction never rests on colour alone. #}
  .compare .yes { color: var(--sl-ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .compare .no { color: var(--sl-ink-muted); }
  {# Scoped to tbody. `tr:last-child` also matched the single row inside
     <thead>, which stripped the header's underline — invisible while that
     header was a filled bar, and a missing rule the moment it stopped being
     one. #}
  .compare tbody tr:last-child td,
  .compare tbody tr:last-child th { border-bottom: none; }

  {# ---- fine print ---- #}
  .fineprint {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
    color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .compare-section + .fineprint {
    margin-top: var(--sl-space-6);
    padding-top: var(--sl-space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  }

  {# Two columns only once there is room for the buy box to stay a real panel
     beside the copy; below that it stacks under it. #}
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .plans .card.hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(280px, 0.5fr);
      gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
      align-items: center;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .plans .card { flex-basis: 100%; padding: var(--sl-space-5) var(--sl-space-4); }
    .plans .card.hero { padding: var(--sl-space-5) var(--sl-space-4); }
  }
{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
  <div class="lead">
    <p class="sl-eyebrow">Choose your coaching pace</p>
    <h1>One analysis engine. {{ "Three" if coach_tier_enabled else "Two" }} ways to use it.</h1>
    <p>Free and Pro run the same analysis and get the same report — the
      metrics table, key-position frames, slow motion, centerline overlays,
      coaching notes, and a practice plan with re-film targets. Free is
      {% if free_per_month <= 0 %}unlimited full reports{% else %}{{ free_per_month }} full report{% if free_per_month != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% if free_matched_refilm %}
      plus a matched re-film{% endif %}
      a month{% endif %}. Pro is {% if pro_per_month <= 0 %}unlimited filming{% else %}up to
      {{ pro_per_month }} analyses a month{% endif %}{% if not coach_tier_enabled %}{% if replay_pro_only %}, plus the
      annotated coach replay — your own footage played back with your
      tracked body, your hand path, and the key numbers appearing at each
      swing event{% endif %}{% if progress_pro_only %},
      plus the progress dashboard that charts every metric session over
      session so you can watch a fix stick{% endif %}{% endif %}.
      {% if coach_tier_enabled %}Coach adds the part nobody else
      does{% if replay_pro_only %}: the annotated replay of every
      swing{% endif %}{% if progress_pro_only %}, the progress dashboard that
      charts every metric session over session{% endif %}, and the proof cycle
      that refuses to call a fix real until a matched re-film says so.
      {# The approved positioning line — the ladder's one-sentence honest
         summary (two-tier design spec, 2026-08-09). Rendered only with the
         ladder itself, and only when both display prices exist, so the
         sentence can never quote a number the cards don't. #}
      {% if coach_price_monthly_text and pro_price_monthly_text %}
      <strong>{{ pro_price_monthly_text.split("/")[0] }} gets you what other
      swing apps sell. {{ coach_price_monthly_text.split("/")[0] }} gets you
      proof that the fix held.</strong>{% endif %}{% endif %}</p>
  </div>

  {% if trend_line %}
  {# Their own numbers, shown only when two sessions of real data exist. #}
  <p class="personal">{{ trend_line }}.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% macro pro_cta(store_href=None, label=None, owned=None) -%}
      {# store_href deep-links the card's own variant so checkout opens on
         the plan that was clicked; without one, the plain product page.
         `owned` says whether this viewer already holds THIS card's plan —
         passed in rather than read off the user, because with two tiers a
         Pro subscriber must still see a live Coach CTA. #}
      {% set already = user.is_pro if owned is none else owned %}
      {% if user and already %}
      <p class="hint">You're on {{ label or "Pro" }} — thanks for the support!</p>
      {% elif user and pro_store_url %}
      <a class="button" href="{{ store_href or pro_store_url }}" data-pro-click>Get {{ label or "Pro" }} on the {{ brand.name }} store</a>
      <p class="hint">Check out with <strong>{{ user.email }}</strong> —
        it unlocks on this account automatically.</p>
      {% elif pro_store_url %}
      {# Anonymous visitor, store configured: send them to checkout.
         Every branch above is gated on `user`, so cold traffic from an ad
         or a shared link fell through to "Log in to upgrade" and converted
         at zero — and that link carried no `next`, so the plan they clicked
         was lost even if they did sign in. Buying first is safe:
         claim_pending_pro attaches a purchase made before the account
         existed, matched on the checkout email. #}
      <a class="button" href="{{ store_href or pro_store_url }}" data-pro-click>Get {{ label or "Pro" }} on the {{ brand.name }} store</a>
      <p class="hint">No account needed to buy — check out, then sign in
        with the same email and it unlocks automatically.</p>
      {% else %}
      {# Purchases go through the Shopify store, and only the store — with
         no store configured there is deliberately nothing to sell here. #}
      <p class="hint">Coming soon.</p>
      {% endif %}
  {%- endmacro %}
  <div class="plans">
    <div class="card hero">
      <div class="hero-plan__copy">
        {% if pro_annual_badge_text %}<span class="badge">{{ pro_annual_badge_text }}</span>{% endif %}
        <h2>Pro — Season Pass</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>{% if pro_per_month <= 0 %}Unlimited swing analyses for a year{% else %}
            Up to {{ pro_per_month }} analyses a month for a year{% endif %}</li>
          <li>Everything Pro includes, all season — and the off-season too</li>
          {% if replay_pro_only and not coach_tier_enabled %}<li>Upgrade and re-film with your annotated coach replay</li>{% endif %}
          <li>One checkout covers the whole year — no monthly decision to remake</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-plan__buy">
        <p class="hero-plan__label">A full year of Pro</p>
        <p class="price">{{ pro_price_annual_text or "Unlimited" }}</p>
        {{ pro_cta(pro_store_url_yearly) }}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Pro — monthly</h2>
      <p class="price">{{ pro_price_monthly_text or "Unlimited" }}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>{% if pro_per_month <= 0 %}Unlimited swing analyses{% else %}
          Up to {{ pro_per_month }} analyses a month{% endif %}</li>
        <li>Everything Pro includes</li>
        {% if store_subscriptions %}
        <li>Subscribe, or buy a single month at a time</li>
        {% else %}
        <li>One month at a time — it simply expires, nothing renews</li>
        {% endif %}
      </ul>
      {{ pro_cta(pro_store_url_monthly) }}
      {% if pro_store_url %}
      <p class="hint">The store shows the available terms, renewal details,
        and total price before payment.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if pro_store_url %}
    {# The Founders Pass exists only as a store purchase (it matches on
       SKU SL-PRO-LIFE, never the variant title) — an install without the
       store configured has no one-payment product to sell, so the card
       would promise something its checkout can't deliver. #}
    <div class="card founders">
      <p class="founders-cap">Capped at the first 100 members</p>
      <h2>Pro — Founders Pass</h2>
      <p class="price">{{ pro_price_lifetime_text or "One payment" }}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>One payment — everything Pro includes, for as long as
          {{ brand.name }} runs</li>
        <li>Never renews, never expires — Founders stay grandfathered
          through every future price change</li>
      </ul>
      {{ pro_cta(pro_store_url_lifetime) }}
      <p class="founders-note">A lifetime product is only honest if we can
        afford to keep running it, so we limit how many Founders Passes
        exist.</p>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if coach_tier_enabled %}
    {# Coach: the upper rung. Rendered only once the ladder is rolled out,
       so the page never offers a plan the store cannot sell. #}
    <div class="card coach">
      <h2>Coach — monthly</h2>
      <p class="price">{{ coach_price_monthly_text or "Everything, proven" }}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Pro</li>
        {% if replay_pro_only %}<li>The annotated coach replay of every swing —
          your own footage with your tracked body, hand path, and the numbers
          at each swing event</li>
        <li>The Swing Pattern — your report names how your swing is built:
          body-led or arm-led, centered or lateral, steady-headed or mobile,
          read straight from your measurements</li>{% endif %}
        {% if progress_pro_only %}<li>The progress dashboard: every metric
          charted session over session, so you can watch a fix hold</li>{% endif %}
        <li>The proof cycle — a pass mark, a matched re-film, and a verdict
          that only counts a change once it survives two checks</li>
      </ul>
      {{ pro_cta(coach_store_url_monthly, "Coach", user.has_coach if user else false) }}
    </div>
    {% if coach_store_url_yearly or coach_price_annual_text %}
    <div class="card coach">
      <h2>Coach — yearly</h2>
      <p class="price">{{ coach_price_annual_text or "Everything, proven" }}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Coach, all season — and the off-season too</li>
        <li>One checkout covers the whole year</li>
      </ul>
      {{ pro_cta(coach_store_url_yearly, "Coach", user.has_coach if user else false) }}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    <div class="card quiet">
      <h2>Free</h2>
      <p class="price">$0</p>
      <ul>
        <li>{% if free_per_month <= 0 %}Unlimited full swing analyses{% elif free_matched_refilm %}{{ free_per_month }} full analys{% if free_per_month == 1 %}is{% else %}es{% endif %}
          + 1 matched re-film each month{% else %}{{ free_per_month }} full swing analys{% if free_per_month == 1 %}is{% else %}es{% endif %}
          every month{% endif %}, forever</li>
        <li>Full report: metrics, key positions, slow motion, overlays</li>
        <li>Coaching notes and a practice plan for every coaching-ready session</li>
        <li>Capture guidance when a clip needs re-filming</li>
